To the passage near us, they call it Tilikêşûr (The Knife
Finger/Cut Finger).

279
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Tilî?
 
Finger?

280
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,000
Tilikêşûr.
 
Tilikêşûr.

281
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Kî der e ew?
 
Where is that?

282
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,000
Eva... vê tilê ye.
 
It is... it is this hill.

283
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Vê tilê? Vê tilê ber avê da ye, bra?
 
This hill? This hill facing the water, brother?

284
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,000
Eywa. Hm.
 
Yes. Hm.

285
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:53,000
Tilikêşûr. Vira... bil esil Sûrkê bi xwe li vîrê jêr bî.
 
Tilikêşûr. Here... originally Surkê itself was down here.

286
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Li jêr bî?
 
It was down below?

287
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
Li jêr bî. Piştî hudûd daket...
 
It was down below. After the border was established...

288
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:59,000
Kuşber bûn ji wê derê hatin vê derê mekan girtin.
 
They were migrants, they came from there and settled here.

289
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:00,000
Eywa.
 
I see.

290
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Û ew geçît jî... ji wê til... hatin...
 
And that passage too... from that hill... they came...

291
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:07,000
Geçît vegeriyan... Geçît vegeriyan.
 
They returned to the passage... returned to the passage.

292
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,000
Û we lûma nav lê dan Tilikêşûr.
 
And that's why they named it Tilikêşûr.

293
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:10,000
Tilikêşûr.
 
Tilikêşûr.

294
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Hm, Tilikêşûr.
 
Hm, Tilikêşûr.

295
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,000
Navê xwa Tilikêşûr e, bes em dibêjin Sûrkê.
 
Its name is Tilikêşûr, but we say Surkê.

296
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:15,000
Em dibêjin Sûrkê. Erê.
 
We say Surkê. Yes.

297
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:17,000
Sûrkê bi çi meşhûr e?
 
What is Surkê famous for?

298
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:20,000
Sûrkê bi tebîeta xwe meşhûr e...
 
Surkê is famous for its nature...

299
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,000
Û teb'en însanê tê da jî... yanî hêdî ye.
 
And naturally the people in it too... meaning, they are
calm/gentle.

300
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:25,000
Û bi ava xwe meşhûr e.
 
And it is famous for its water.

301
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,000
Bi pezî meşhûr e.
 
It is famous for livestock.

302
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,000
Bi pezê we jî pir e.
 
Your livestock is plentiful too.

303
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Pêz meşhûr e, bi meşhûr e.
 
Livestock is famous, it is famous for it.

304
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:35,000
Û teb'en va heşt destan lo jê zêde deng dayî, şixul tê da
pir e.
 
And naturally, these eight hands (manual labor) have made a
name for themselves, there is a lot of work here.

305
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:40,000
Yanî însan... kê nekaribe bidî... dibê yarit em ji Sûrkê re
nehiştibana.
 
Meaning, a person... whoever cannot give (work)... says "I
wish we hadn't stayed for Surkê."

306
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,000
Erdê we avî ne, ne wilo?
 
Your lands are irrigated, aren't they?

307
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,000
Erd avî ne.
 
The lands are irrigated.

308
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:45,000
Erdê we avî ne, her kes di nav milkê xwe de dixebite.
 
Your lands are irrigated, everyone works within their own
property.

309
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:49,000
Salê çend mewsim hûn diçînin? Mesela perezga radibin du yara
fasulye, tiştî hîn...
 
How many seasons do you plant per year? For example, during
migration season, do you harvest beans twice, or other
things...

310
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Em du fasla diçînin. Bi fasla em radikin... zivistan tê
genim diçînin.
 
We plant two seasons. In the season we harvest... when
winter comes we plant wheat.

311
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Xidre diçînin.
 
You plant vegetables.

312
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:58,000
Xidre diçînin, xidrê payîzê wek qernebî û qernebîta, mesela
xasa...
 
We plant vegetables, autumn vegetables like cauliflower and
broccoli, for example lettuce...

313
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
Hemû tişt tê.
 
Everything grows.

314
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Maşallah, saeta we xweş.
 
Mashallah, bless you.

315
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Wela xelkê Sûrkê baş e, ew jî wek miletê Qirzêlê û Basûtê
her kes milkê xwe da dixebite.
 
By God, the people of Surkê are good, just like the people
of Qirzel and Basut, everyone works on their own property.

316
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Erê, erê.
 
Yes, yes.

317
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

318
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Xalo, min kê solek din ji te bikira pirskirin.
 
Uncle, I wanted to ask you another question.

319
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:13,000
Nuha vê derê Batmanê me go me'rûf bî.
 
Now, here, Batman (a local figure or spot) was famous, as we
said.

320
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Batmanê jî noka av heye yan hişk bûye?
 
Does Batman still have water or has it dried up?

321
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,000
Hişk bûye, ne?
 
It dried up, didn't it?

322
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Hişk e, ne?
 
It is dry, isn't it?

323
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Hişk e.
 
It is dry.

324
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,000
Berê av li vê derê pir bî...
 
Before, there was a lot of water here...

325
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:23,000
Xişim xidre diçandin, xidrê xwe, bîstanê xwe, gi diçandin.
 
They planted a lot of vegetables, their greens, their
gardens, they planted everything.

326
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:27,000
Maşallah milkê cem we jî yanî... neha vê derê rast zeytûn
nehatin.
 
Mashallah, the property near you as well... meaning... right
here olives haven't come yet.

327
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Zeytûnê xwe pir kîbar ne yanî. Darê maşallah çûwal didin.
 
Its olives are very fine. The trees, mashallah, yield sacks
(of olives).

328
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Yê avê didin bi reş û şîn.
 
Those who water them get both black and green ones.

329
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Bi reş û şîn didin, ne?
 
They give black and green ones, right?

330
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

331
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:38,000
Maşallah, saeta we xweş. Xwedê emrê we dirêj bide. Xwedê
destê wa ser we ra bigire.
 
Mashallah, bless you. May God give you a long life. May God
protect you.

332
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:42,000
Vê derê zîkrayatê we giya hene. Em gi hatin, em di vir ra
derbas dibûn. Ez...
 
Here, you have all your memories. We all came, we used to
pass through here. I...

333
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:46,000
Ez... awcî masiyan bûm, ez rûbirû li vê derê bûm. Ber herqê
me masi digirtin.
 
I... I was a fisherman, I was right across here. We used to
catch fish by the stream.

334
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:49,000
Rûbirû Xwedê, em di vir ra diçûn. Şev, seet yek, dudo,
sîsiyo em tê ra diçûn.
 
Facing God, we used to go through here. At night, one
o'clock, two, three o'clock, we went through here.

335
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Erê wela.
 
Yes, by God.

336
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,000
Seeta we xweş. Xwedê emrê we dirêj bide.
 
Bless you. May God give you a long life.

337
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,000
Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

338
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:58,000
Gotin ne we hene? Nika milet ra silav ke bişîne. Nika bibin
çi, te gotin we hene?
 
Do you have anything to say? Send greetings to the people
now. What will become of things now, do you have any words?

339
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Saeta we xweş, Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
Bless you, may God be pleased with you.

340
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:01,000
Ser çava, ti jî xweş.
 
You're welcome (Upon my eyes), you are also good.

341
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:03,000
Saeta we xweş, Xwedê ji Pêxember ji we razî be.
 
Bless you, may God and the Prophet be pleased with you.

342
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Em her carek wextsez wextsez em evê bibînin hana...
 
Whenever we see this unexpectedly...

343
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:07,000
Înşallah, înşallah.
 
God willing, God willing.

344
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:08,000
Û...
 
And...

345
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:11,000
Silav ji miletê Kurd Ewrupa ra û ji gi dera ra.
 
Greetings to the Kurdish people in Europe and everywhere.

346
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:13,000
Em çar parçan silav dikin.
 
We greet all four parts (of Kurdistan).

347
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:16,000
Li gi dera, her yekî Kurd li kî derê be silavê me jê re
hene.
 
Everywhere, wherever a Kurd may be, they have our greetings.

348
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:19,000
Çavê giya maç dikim. Xwedê we giya bixefilîne.
 
I kiss everyone's eyes. May God protect you all.

349
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,000
Amîn.
 
Amen.

350
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:26,000
Erê û... naha ew rû jî yekî jî mera deng kir, birakî me. Ew
jî meşrûhek xwa vekiriye.
 
Yes and... now over there someone called out to us, a
brother of ours. He has also opened a project.

351
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,000
Dê be were îlanokê mar çêke.
 
He said come and make an advertisement for us.

352
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Dê be Ebu Azad, em ten vîdeoyê te seyr dikin.
 
He said Abu Azad, we only watch your videos.

353
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:34,000
Te dê be were meşrûa veke. Dê be me jî hat meşrû vekir,
tekey îlan ke mar çêke.
 
He said come and present the project. He said we also came
and opened a project, just make an ad for us.

354
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,000
Migo ez bi çavê xwe warim.
 
I said I will come with my own eyes (happily).

355
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Meşrûa vekin. Milo miletê gunda... ne sefîl be. Milo...
 
Open projects. So that the village people... are not
destitute. So that...

356
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Di şixul kevin, di kar kevin. Çi warşê xeyata dibe, çi
me'melê plastîk dibe...
 
So they get into jobs, get into work. Whether it's a sewing
workshop, a plastic factory...

357
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Çi me'melê şîşê zeytê dibe... Ewin çi va dikin, va kin.
 
Whether it's an olive oil bottle factory... Whatever they
do, let them do it.

358
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:50,000
Ne her gundekî da hebe, miletê gundê pê sebeb bibe.
 
So that in every village, it becomes a cause (for staying)
for the village people.

359
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:55,000
Sebeb î tenê ye. Neha... şebab xercê me kêm ne. Şebab gi
çûn, kar tine, gi çûn... awe...
 
That is the only reason. Now... our youth expenses aren't
low. The youth all left, there is no work, they all went...
uh...

360
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Bi xerîbiyê ketin.
 
They fell into living abroad.

361
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:59,000
Werin... noka ji vir tekî ro here Efrîn.
 
Come on... from here go straight to Afrin.

362
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:01,000
Efrîn jî 50 kîlometre ye.
 
Afrin is also 50 kilometers away.

363
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:05,000
Dê akî ro em Efrînê bişixulim... dûr e.
 
Should I go to work in Afrin from here... it's far.

364
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:13,000
Erê, avo naha li vê derê jî... bimênin heta dawî vîdeo. Em
naha em derbas bin lextan xweş kîbar, emê nav gund war
çêkin.
 
Yes, friends, stay here as well... until the end of the
video. We will now pass through some very nice spots, we
will film inside the village for you.

365
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:16,000
Xol vêra boyboy ke.
 
Friend, honk the horn here.

366
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Boyboy kin vêra.
 
Honk the horn here.

367
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:25,000
Maşallah Sûrkê... Sûrkê pir xweş e, kîbar e.
 
Mashallah, Surkê... Surkê is very nice, it is beautiful.

368
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:30,000
Wele min tim silav da digot akê werim hewşek xol derê ni
bigirim ber... berî tel.
 
By God, I always said greetings, saying I will come and
capture a courtyard view nearby... near the hill.

369
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:33,000
Ew derê.
 
That place.

370
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:35,000
Saet xweş, Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
Bless you, may God be pleased with you.

371
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Henderî min li Sûrkê hez dikira, tim dihatim masiyan, min
digot akê hewşek xol wir bigirim.
 
Because I loved Surkê so much, I always came for fish, I
said I would capture a courtyard view there.

372
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:42,000
Weleh gundekî pir xweş e.
 
By God, it is a very nice village.

373
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:43,000
Lê...
 
But...

374
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:45,000
Maşallah gundekî pir xweş e.
 
Mashallah, it is a very nice village.

375
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:48,000
Ez diginim vê derê, soq madiginim nav gundê xwe.
 
I'm reaching this place, soon we will reach inside our
village.

376
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:52,000
Yanî xêr e, min zîkrayatê min li vir pir nin, ez tim dihatim
vê derê.
 
Meaning it's good, I don't have many memories here, (but) I
always came here.

377
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:55,000
Em çûçik bînîn, babkê xwe rehmetî ra dihatim.
 
When we were small, I used to come with my late father.

378
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:58,000
Erê wele.
 
Yes, by God.

379
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:18,000
[Music playing, car driving through the village]
 
[Music playing, car driving through the village]

380
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:21,000
[Car slowing down, ambient noise]
 
[Car slowing down, ambient noise]

381
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:41,000
[Car driving continues with music]
 
[Car driving continues with music]

382
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Weleh... hewş kîbor da... ka binêrin.
 
[Music continues]

383
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:08,000
Weleh... hewş kîbor da... ka binêrin.
 
By God... a neat courtyard... look here.

384
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:28,000
Xweş sehne, şiniyetî da pir e.
 
A beautiful scene, there is a lot of greenery.

385
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:50,000
Maşallah, çi hewş kîbor e hey, of babê of, heyata.
 
Mashallah, what a neat courtyard, oh man oh, it's life.

386
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:27,000
Maşallah maşallah, cesûr kero maşallah... hê maşallah...
maşallah.
 
Mashallah mashallah, brave donkey [car] mashallah... hey
mashallah... mashallah.

387
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:35,000
Te çû ye? Are elhemdulilah tîk kasoxê dikê o...
 
Did it go? Yes, praise be to God, he is shearing a little...

388
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:39,000
Erê li vî derê jî birokî me kasoxê dikê?
 
Yes, but here too a bit... are you shearing [the sheep]?

389
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:40,000
Dorê şemsî ye ne.
 
It is the solar turn [season for shearing], isn't it.

390
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:44,000
Lê her wext ki wext ki, tikê di nava av bikê?
 
But every time, whenever, do you put it in the water?

391
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:45,000
Hotîkê?
 
What?

392
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:48,000
Ava çelê da dikê paqij kê?
 
Do you put it in the river water to clean it?

393
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:49,000
Çelê da na?
 
In the river, no?

394
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

395
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:55,000
Çelê da dor dest ki nî ewan e.
 
It's not the turn to handle them in the river.

396
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Rind e, sato te xweş.
 
Good, health to you [literally: may your hour be pleasant].

397
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:04,000
Ew dar wekî benîadem işta çivan porê xwe çê dikin, tikey
darê jî wusa bikê, tikê şake, vade, pak bikê.
 
Those trees are like human beings, just like how they fix
their hair, you have to do the trees like that too, you have
to comb, prune, and clean them.

398
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Erê wallah.
 
Yes, by God.

399
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:08,000
Reg dijwar e yan hewa?
 
Is the vein/root tough or the weather?

400
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:09,000
Belê, gellek dijwar e.
 
Yes, very tough.

401
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Ka la la ez dîtya bikim la.
 
Let me, let me try/see, man.

402
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:16,000
Meqesê te... meqesê te çi tûjî ye, ow biye...
 
Your scissors... your scissors are so sharp, oh it
happened...

403
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:18,000
(Laughs) Dest neynê.
 
(Laughs) Don't touch it.

404
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:22,000
We ke wî gotî, min bi nav nekin...
 
Like he said, don't mention me...

405
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:25,000
Haw û tembûr qe nemeşîn.
 
The song and the tambourine didn't go well together.

406
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:27,000
Cehre û meqes û nizanim çi vo...
 
The jar and scissors and I don't know what else...

407
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:29,000
Her yekî karê ber destê babê xwe girtiye ro na?
 
Everyone has taken up their father's trade, haven't they?

408
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:32,000
Erê erê, tiştê ku jê dûr nekeve, jê dûr nekeve.
 
Yes yes, the thing you shouldn't distance yourself from,
don't distance yourself from it.

409
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Lê canê qena, canê xwe yo...
 
But the soul is convinced, it's his own soul...

410
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:37,000
Canê... canê to xwedê.
 
The soul... the soul is yours, God.

411
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Lê em tê werbun.
 
But we got used to it.

412
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:41,000
Ewanî fêkî... nîvan o...
 
Those fruits... half of them...

413
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Lê nîvan jama miqeddes e.
 
But the middle/half is a sacred group.

414
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:44,000
Ê awê ta, têbê meqesê ta na xewn da.
 
And yours, you say your scissors are not sleepy/dull.

415
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:46,000
No na şixulî ye.
 
No, it is not for work.

416
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:47,000
Bigire.
 
Take it.

417
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,000
A...
 
Uh...

418
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:51,000
Ne ne şixulî ye.
 
No, it is not for work.

419
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:54,000
Guh wekî gihaye têdana.
 
It's like grass is inside it [the wool].

420
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:56,000
Erê erê, zivî gundî ye.
 
Yes yes, it's the winter of the village.

421
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:58,000
Ev jî ne qulûyî ye?
 
Is this not matted/dirty?

422
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Tiştê quluyî tîne?
 
Does it bring matted things?

423
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:02,000
Cefoyî gihaye, cefoyî gihaye.
 
It's dry grass, it's dry grass.

424
00:33:02,000 --> 00:33:05,000
Tiştê quluyî tîne.
 
It brings matted things.

425
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:08,000
Tekê pîçê merdî şîn...
 
It requires a bit of man's [strength]...

426
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:10,000
Tekê bi hindir bê te voye aw bikê.
 
It needs to come from inside so you can do that.

427
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:12,000
Bi şixulî ne.
 
It's with work/effort.

428
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:14,000
Ev na çin e? Sêv na çin e têda?
 
Are these not going? Are there no apples going in there?

429
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,000
No no no, wekî awaye me got çi dan dika.
 
No no no, like that, we said what gives grain.

430
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Dan dika ne?
 
Does it give grain?

431
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Hewa çaka erdê.
 
Like hitting the ground.

432
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:20,000
Maro çaka erdê bi? No te der?
 
Did the snake hit the ground? Not outside?

433
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Neş, çima tê der.
 
No, why would it be outside.

434
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:22,000
Çû ye ev?
 
It's gone, this one?

435
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Wala.
 
By God.

436
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:27,000
Ko ez pirra bibim, amê biçînin, amê qena... çûn dero amê
biçînin.
 
Let me get full [get ready], we will plant, we will act...
going outside we will plant.

437
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Awo tekitî ça... awo da biçîne çi...
 
That one alone how... that one to plant what...

438
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Qutîka da ne.
 
In the boxes?

439
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:30,000
Qutîka da ne.
 
In the boxes, yes.

440
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:31,000
Ê paşê?
 
And then?

441
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,000
Paşê awo derxin der, tê tenekokî mezin.
 
Then take that out, put it in a big tin can.

442
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:34,000
Wala wala wa ye.
 
By God, by God, that's it.

443
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:37,000
Maşallah... keçik in an çi... win çi dikin lê?
 
Mashallah... are they girls or what... what are you doing,
hey?

444
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:39,000
Heyda emrê min heyda.
 
Come on, my life, come on.

445
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:40,000
Win çi dikin?
 
What are you doing?

446
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Te feqîra naçin mektebê?
 
You poor things don't go to school?

447
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:43,000
Çima dan mektebê.
 
Why, they gave [sent us] to school.

448
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:45,000
Heye ne? Sofî çendê ne?
 
Is there? What grade are you in?

449
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Yekê.
 
First.

450
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:47,000
Te yekê?
 
You are in first?

451
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:48,000
Te herfa zanê?
 
Do you know the letters?

452
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:49,000
Lê.
 
Yes.

453
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Hade wa be, te destê xwe birîn bikê o.
 
Come here then, you hurt your hand, oh.

454
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:53,000
Ha ha ha ha.
 
Ha ha ha ha.

455
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Te destê xwe birîn bikê. Hade herfa wa be te zanê?
 
You hurt your hand. Come, show the letters if you know them?

456
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:58,000
Dê. Dê wa be.
 
Come on. Come on, come here.

457
00:33:58,000 --> 00:33:59,000
Awo rûkena car nîne.
 
That smiling one is not here right now.

458
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Kî herfa zanê?
 
Who knows the letters?

459
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:01,000
Pelatî me.
 
I am Pelat.

460
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:02,000
Navê te çiye?
 
What is your name?

461
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Hêlîn.
 
Helin.

462
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:04,000
Hêlîn?
 
Helin?

463
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Ka wa... wa vera vir... wa vera vir. Dê qîskê rû boyboy ke
wele kî bê pî ke dê.
 
Let me... come here... come here. Come, kiss the face, bye-
bye, yes, whoever says do it.

464
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:12,000
Dê boyboy ke. Dê Hêlînê boyboy ke. Dê tu jî berfê xwe bar de
bike boyboy ke dê.
 
Come say bye-bye. Come Helin, say bye-bye. Come, you too
drop your snow [ice cream/foam], say bye-bye.

465
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:13,000
Hingiştik sofî yekê ne.
 
You are all in first grade.

466
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:16,000
Maşallah, Xwedê ji we ra bihêle, Xwedê mehfaze ke.
 
Mashallah, may God keep them for you, may God protect them.

467
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:19,000
Şatêr bin o, manî bi taxtir bin, enseh bin. Temam?
 
Be smart, meaning be doctors, be engineers. Okay?

468
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:21,000
Lê?
 
Yes?

469
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:24,000
Bê siba mezin bibin, elqê sêr kin feqîra.
 
Let them grow up tomorrow, let them serve the poor.

470
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:25,000
Erê wallah.
 
Yes, by God.

471
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:27,000
Da marokê gundo çikorî bikê.
 
So the village snake [sly/smart person] does what.

472
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Haa wallah korî gundo, işta wane ye.
 
Oh by God, the village boy, that is how it is.

473
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Bas xweş ca.
 
But a nice place.

474
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:34,000
Daworî mera hebê, tiştî mera hebê, xweş e li gundo.
 
If we have livestock, if we have things, it is nice in the
village.

475
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Erê wallah.
 
Yes, by God.

476
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:38,000
Maşallah, çi hewş kîbor di virdana.
 
Mashallah, what a neat courtyard over here.

477
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:39,000
Lê?
 
Yes?

478
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:40,000
Êê.
 
Yeah.

479
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:41,000
Erê wallah.
 
Yes, by God.

480
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:43,000
Afare vir gon tine.
 
There is no fold [for animals] here.

481
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Goşoş bigon.
 
[Unintelligible - maybe specific name or task].

482
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Lê?
 
Yes?

483
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:47,000
Tiştkê deroş bera ne?
 
Something... [Unintelligible].

484
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:50,000
Inşallah nîzik da jêk jome yekuder anû çêkim.
 
God willing, soon I will make one nearby too.

485
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:52,000
Ekê li gundî Sûrke rûnim.
 
I will settle one in the village of Surke.

486
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:53,000
Inşallah.
 
God willing.

487
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Jê arendê ane.
 
It's from over there.

488
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:56,000
Bere arendê weke... bere weşke.
 
Look over there like... look at that.

489
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:57,000
Arendê rol ver rûniştine?
 
Are they sitting over there?

490
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:58,000
A xaçxalî ye hene.
 
Uh, Aunt Xaçxalî [Hatice-Xalil?] is there.

491
00:34:58,000 --> 00:34:59,000
Wala?
 
Really?

492
00:34:59,000 --> 00:35:00,000
Jê 'emmero hene.
 
From 'Emmer [Omer?] too.

493
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:01,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

494
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,000
Her werrekî wêtî wira.
 
Every way/road comes there.

495
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:05,000
Jê 'emmero, jê xaçxalîl, jê arendê gi hatin ver rûniştine.
 
From 'Emmer, from Xaçxalîl, from everywhere they all came
and sat there.

496
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:07,000
Ê be'dîno li vir tenê ne?
 
And Be'dîno is alone here?

497
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:09,000
No be'dîno li vir tine ne.
 
No, Be'dîno is not here.

498
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:12,000
No? Lo ne hem tim li vî derê ne, sok mi hem ji vî derê ne.
 
No? But aren't we all here, look we are all from here too.

499
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:13,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

500
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:15,000
Cemaetî wa mûsa gel vira.
 
Musa's group is with him here.

501
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Ah, zotira tim da hatim vî derê.
 
Ah, earlier I came here completely.

502
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:19,000
Satê ta xweş, qay o, xwedê ji te razî be.
 
Have a good time, okay, may God be pleased with you.

503
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:20,000
Dûr am rûnim.
 
Let's sit far away.

504
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:22,000
Saet xweş.
 
Have a good time.

505
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:26,000
Bro mala Mistefayê Silêmê ne li Sûrke?
 
Brother, isn't this Mustafa Sileman's house in Surke?

506
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:29,000
Maşallah bato çiqas li cema hev pirr ne?
 
Mashallah, how many ducks are there together?

507
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:30,000
Bato...
 
Ducks...

508
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:31,000
Avê mha hewand ne?
 
Did they shelter in the water?

509
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:32,000
Hêlînê dikin?
 
Are they nesting?

510
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:33,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

511
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:35,000
Wala.
 
Really.

512
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:36,000
Hê.
 
Yeah.

513
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:39,000
Wala hşînî çiqas çakiri pîşe.
 
By God, how well the greenery has grown.

514
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:40,000
Maşallah maşallah.
 
Mashallah mashallah.

515
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,000
Şînî e, ti dikê bi ser keve.
 
It's greenery, you have to nurture it.

516
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:44,000
Maşallah, maşallah.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

517
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:45,000
Hehe.
 
Hehe.

518
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:46,000
Ê birî ovê heye cema hewşê da?
 
Is there a water well in the courtyard group?

519
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

520
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Maşallah avû nû çiqso hşînî rinde ha vana.
 
Mashallah, the water and the new greenery are so good like
this.

521
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Î noka... ne magû bistan he... çil û dar û rimduweşî ye.
 
And now... didn't we say there is a garden... forty trees
and it is lush.

522
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:57,000
Ê ne wa bo hîne xweş bo.
 
And if it wasn't like that, it wouldn't be nice.

523
00:35:57,000 --> 00:35:59,000
Ê wa xweş e.
 
Yeah, that is nice.

524
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:00,000
Ê tebîetek pir xweş li vira heye.
 
There is a very nice nature here.

525
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Selam aleykum.
 
Peace be upon you.

526
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:04,000
Xalo çi kêfî rûniştî ye gelê... ta dît?
 
Uncle, with what pleasure he is sitting there folks... did
you see?

527
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:07,000
Î gundo, emrê xwe dirêj in o maşallah.
 
This village, their lives are long, mashallah.

528
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:10,000
Hana cewikî xweş, pak, li hewşê rûniştina.
 
Like this, a nice, clean atmosphere, sitting in the
courtyard.

529
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:11,000
Selam aleykum.
 
Peace be upon you.

530
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:12,000
Ser çava.
 
Upon my eyes [You are welcome].

531
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:13,000
Merheba, merheba.
 
Hello, hello.

532
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Tu çû te?
 
How are you?

533
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:15,000
Hemdillah tu çû ye?
 
Thank God, how are you?

534
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:16,000
Wala elhemdulillah ji xwedê ra.
 
By God, praise be to God.

535
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:17,000
Hal kêf?
 
How is your mood?

536
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:20,000
Wala xol û kêf keyfê te ye. Tey xwedêyî rûyê...
 
By God, the mood and pleasure is your pleasure. You came
from God's face [blessing]...

537
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:22,000
Ya şukim, xwedê emrê ki dirêj bide te.
 
Oh thanks, may God give you a long life.

538
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,000
Te serê xwe birîn kirî?
 
Did you cut your hair?

539
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Êê.
 
Yeah.

540
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:26,000
Xwedê emrê ki dirêj bide te.
 
May God give you a long life.

541
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Şalû şapik... işta hevo, awê mey hevo, kûre mey işta...
 
Traditional clothes... like this, ours like this, our boy
like this...

542
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:31,000
Kûre kurmancî...
 
A Kurdish boy...

543
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:34,000
Şal û şapik, kepşal û wer be, kê tûrîsê be he be.
 
Traditional clothes, hat and all, whoever is a tourist
should have it.

544
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:35,000
Na wey?
 
Isn't it?

545
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:35,000
E bes diloqi ta tine ye.
 
Yeah?

546
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:36,000
E bes diloqi ta tine ye.
 
But you don't have the tassel/vest.

547
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:39,000
Diloq, wala hebû, diloq dûr dir e.
 
The tassel/vest, by God I had one, the vest is far away.

548
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:40,000
Maşallah, xwedê emrê ki dirêj bide te.
 
Mashallah, may God give you a long life.

549
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:41,000
Ehlê we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

550
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:43,000
Wala wano ma, em eresta we hatin, te kasoxê dikê?
 
By God, we came towards you, are you shearing?

551
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:44,000
Ser çava.
 
You are welcome.

552
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Ma go em werin hewşê derxin.
 
We said let's come and film/bring out the courtyard.

553
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:47,000
Ser serî min.
 
Upon my head [Welcome].

554
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:49,000
Maşallah, xolû heşînayî cem we pir e.
 
Mashallah, Uncle, there is a lot of greenery with you.

555
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:50,000
Hêşînî pir e.
 
Greenery is plentiful.

556
00:36:50,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Wa bîr lê xistine xolû?
 
Did you dig a well, Uncle?

557
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,000
Bîr jî heye.
 
There is a well too.

558
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Maşallah maşallah.
 
Mashallah mashallah.

559
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:55,000
Rind e.
 
Good.

560
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:57,000
Are.
 
Yes.

561
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:58,000
Pezî we jî heye xolû?
 
Do you have sheep too, Uncle?

562
00:36:58,000 --> 00:36:59,000
Pez jî heye.
 
There are sheep too.

563
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:00,000
Êê.
 
Yeah.

564
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:04,000
Xolû, maşallah em nava gundê Sûrke digerin, em teswîr dikin.
 
Uncle, mashallah we are walking in Surke village, we are
filming.

565
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:05,000
Ziraşiye.
 
It's agriculture.

566
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:10,000
Tebîetê, cografyayê, em pêş milet dikin, da pir milet ma jî
heye dûr çûye.
 
Nature, geography, we show the people, because we have many
people who went far away.

567
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:11,000
Meleke be Hesen.
 
[Unintelligible, possibly a name or place].

568
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:14,000
Dibe gundî ma mera bi sewirînin, em gundîkî di wer
disewirînin.
 
They say film our village for us, we are filming a village
from here.

569
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:15,000
Temam.
 
Okay.

570
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Yane ta çina sihetê didê milet.
 
Meaning what advice do you give the people?

571
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Es sela baş, milet gi ro dişînim.
 
Good peace, I send it to all the people.

572
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:19,000
Êwa.
 
Yes.

573
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:22,000
Û miletê her Kurd, li kuder e, ser ser û ser çava.
 
And every Kurdish people, wherever they are, upon my head
and upon my eyes.

574
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:23,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

575
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:27,000
Û her kes... ki biçûyani, ez...
 
And everyone... who goes... I...

576
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:31,000
Yane te çina sihetê didê milet, te dibê werin, me tên?
 
Meaning what advice do you give the people, do you say come,
don't come?

577
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:35,000
Wala î konê werê, î nikonê milû netê, î şêkê ji hewa xera.
 
By God, the one who can should come, the one who can't
should not come, the suspicion is also bad for them.

578
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Awa î şêkê ji heye.
 
That one has suspicion too.

579
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:37,000
Ê me hem nûrin.
 
And we are all light [or settled/happy].

580
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:38,000
Ne? Ez nûrim.
 
No? I am light.

581
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:39,000
Em te dera danîn.
 
We put you outside.

582
00:37:39,000 --> 00:37:43,000
Em bes em wekî vê mûsîd ovêt em derkevin emê fasid.
 
We just, like this season wants, we go out, we will spoil
[if we stay inside].

583
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:46,000
Li vê axê çêbîn, emê li vê axê jî bimrin.
 
We were born on this soil, we will die on this soil too.

584
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:47,000
Are.
 
Yes.

585
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:47,000
Xwedê emrê ki dirêj bide te.
 
Yes.

586
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:49,000
Xwedê emrê ki dirêj bide te.
 
May God give you a long life.

587
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:49,000
Xwedê wekî dibê wa nakê berdesta inşallah.
 
May you be healthy too.

588
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:52,000
Xwedê wekî dibê wa nakê berdesta inşallah.
 
May God, as they say, not make you dependent on anyone God
willing.

589
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:53,000
Sax bî.
 
Be healthy.

590
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Ew jî kulfetê min e.
 
That is my wife/family.

591
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:57,000
Xwedê, xwedê we ji hev ra bihêle, xwedê destê we ser we ra
bigre.
 
God, may God keep you for each other, may God hold His hand
over you.

592
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:01,000
Are wallah, we lê vî derê em cema abo Mihemed ne.
 
Yes by God, look here we are with brother Mohammed's group.

593
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:05,000
Maşallah hewşek kîbor, delal heye, hêşînahiyek xwe pir e.
 
Mashallah, a neat, beautiful courtyard, lots of greenery.

594
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:09,000
Ew jî nava bistan e, dor... dor belê xwo gi waşîn e.
 
That is inside the garden, around... around indeed it is all
grassy.

595
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:12,000
Wextî heşînayî war vî dare pir rind e.
 
The time of greenery coming here is very good.

596
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:15,000
Vê gundî kî deweta dikê, bikê tînîn vî derê teswîr dikin.
 
Whoever makes a wedding in this village, brings the bride
here to film.

597
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:18,000
Xinderî heşînî xwo rind e, û kîbor e.
 
Its greenery is very good, and neat.

598
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Xalo silava ji lawikê xwe ra bişîne Elmanya.
 
Uncle, send greetings to your son in Germany.

599
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:23,000
Ez ji vir da silama dişînim heta bi Elmanya...
 
I send greetings from here all the way to Germany...

600
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:24,000
Hozan...
 
Hozan...

601
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Li bunyana bajarê Almanya...
 
In the building of the city of Germany...

602
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:28,000
Û her şebekî...
 
And every network/person...

603
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:33,000
Her şebekî li Almanya, her yekî ji Sûrye çûye, silamê min ji
giştika ra heye.
 
Every person in Germany, everyone who went from Syria, my
greetings to all of them.

604
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:34,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

605
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:35,000
Ê bigrîne mabo şer.
 
And take it, there is no war.

606
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:37,000
Xwedê giyo mehfaze ke.
 
May God protect them all.

607
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:40,000
Xwedê ji te razî be, xwedê emrê ki dirêj bide te.
 
May God be pleased with you, may God give you a long life.

608
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:43,000
Xolû noka win gundo... ew cem we heye bistan heye win
diçinin?
 
Uncle, now in the village... do you have a garden that you
plant?

609
00:38:43,000 --> 00:38:45,000
Livira erd zîraî ye yo.
 
Here the land is agricultural.

610
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:46,000
Livira kanî heye.
 
There is a spring here.

611
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:47,000
Hmm.
 
Hmm.

612
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:50,000
Livira cîyê pîvaz û baxçe ye.
 
Here is the place for onions and gardens.

613
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:57,000
Livira... lê bistana jî diçînin, qewina jî diçînin, zebeşa
jî diçînin, are.
 
Here... yes, we plant gardens too, we plant melons too, we
plant watermelons too, yes.

614
00:38:57,000 --> 00:39:01,000
Wala mletîo cam hebe xêr û bêr e maşallah.
 
By God, if the people have glass [greenhouses/frames], it is
goodness and bounty mashallah.

615
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:05,000
Ê wala elhemdulillah bi xêr e, ê her yekî bi şuxulê bi xêr
e.
 
Yeah, by God, praise be to God, it is good, everyone with
work is good.

616
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:07,000
Bes î bê şixulî ne bi xêr e.
 
But the one without work is not good.

617
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:10,000
Do coqê taxaw keta sehet dav dîdyo ro bî, te zotir...
 
If you fall asleep until ten o'clock like that, you
sooner...

618
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:11,000
Zotir rizq sibe tê ne?
 
Sooner, sustenance comes in the morning, right?

619
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:12,000
Na'am.
 
Yes.

620
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:16,000
Dê bê sibe zû te rabî, meriv xeyret, sibe zû şeş şeşa rabî.
 
You must get up early in the morning, man needs effort, get
up early at six, six o'clock.

621
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:17,000
Xwedê rizqê te bide.
 
God gives you your sustenance.

622
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:19,000
Xwedê rizqî gindê vêra bişîne.
 
May God send sustenance to the village here.

623
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:23,000
Bes mi xew kir, nîvro bî, xelkê gişta şixulê xwe...
 
But if I slept, it became noon, all the people did their
work...

624
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:24,000
Eke em çi şixulî bikin?
 
What work should we do then?

625
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:26,000
No, xelq... no, tiştê xêrê no bînî.
 
No, people... no, you won't see anything good.

626
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:27,000
No?
 
No?

627
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:28,000
Lo şixul tune ye lo?
 
But is there no work?

628
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:30,000
Lo şixul te bi şixulê hebe...
 
But work, if you have work...

629
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:31,000
Şixul behr e?
 
Work is an ocean?

630
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:32,000
Şixul behr e, are.
 
Work is an ocean, yes.

631
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:33,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

632
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:37,000
Xo dêk gotinê te hene, te kî silavkî ji lokî xwo Elmanya ro
bişînê?
 
Auntie, do you have any words, will you send a greeting to
your son in Germany?

633
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:39,000
Silavê mi j gor ra hene.
 
My greetings to them all.

634
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:43,000
Xwedê j gor ra bêle, qapîkê xêrê veke.
 
May God say yes to them, open the door of goodness.

635
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Xwedê mezin... Mhemed... cam... afza ke.
 
God is great... Mohammed... glass [? or name]... protect.

636
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,000
Won goj mahfaza ke.
 
Protect them all too.

637
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:50,000
Xwedê emrê ki dirêj bide te, xwedê tenakê berdesta.
 
May God give you a long life, may God not make you
dependent.

638
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:53,000
Xwedê ta û xolû ji hev ra bêle, û xwedê we bixapilîne.
 
May God keep you and Uncle for each other, and may God
deceive [protect/entertain] you.

639
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:54,000
Sax be.
 
Be healthy.

640
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:56,000
Maşallah maşallah.
 
Mashallah mashallah.

641
00:39:56,000 --> 00:39:58,000
Wa xurû germek e... xolû na mketin çêla?
 
It is somewhat hot... Uncle, didn't we fall into the mist?

642
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Wala hîr û çêla ye, hîr û çêla ye.
 
By God, it is fog and mist, it is fog and mist.

643
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:03,000
Yan îro dinya sêhr e.
 
Or today the weather is warm.

644
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:04,000
Erê sêhr e.
 
Yes, it is warm.

645
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Îro ki şirovek biguheriya.
 
Today the weather has changed a bit.

646
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Yanî hewa germ e.
 
Yes.

647
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:08,000
Yanî hewa germ e.
 
Meaning the weather is warm.

648
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:13,000
Û sal jî... yanî heste du sal in baran kêm zêîf in.
 
And the season... you know, for two years the rain has been
scarce and weak.

649
00:40:13,000 --> 00:40:14,000
Ceffaf çêbûne?
 
Was there a drought?

650
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:19,000
Çîçke ceffaf heye û deyaqandin heye di milet da yanî.
 
There is a bit of drought and hardship among the people.

651
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:20,000
Aywa.
 
Yes.

652
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Ew jî rehma Xwedê ye, ne bi ê min û ne bi ê te ye. Xwedê
inşallah ew bibe.
 
That is God's mercy, it's not up to me or you. God willing,
it will happen.

653
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Belê, baran hatibû, ew hîn xweş bibe îsal ne?
 
Yes, rain had come, it will be even better this year, right?

654
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:31,000
Ew ji ber xweş bibe erê, inşallah.
 
It will be better than before, yes, God willing.

655
00:40:31,000 --> 00:40:37,000
Çîçke ceffaf çêbî milet pê tesîr bî. Dar ber, hişinahî têne.
Dora me jî zêde wek berê namîne.
 
If a bit of drought happens, people are affected. Trees,
crops, greenery suffer. Our surroundings don't stay as lush
as before.

656
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:43,000
Dar hebe ew jî çêdibe, rutûbet çêdibe, yanî cew xweş dibe.
 
If there are trees, it helps, humidity is created, meaning
the atmosphere becomes pleasant.

657
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:44,000
Inşallah Xwedê bişîne.
 
God willing, God will send it.

658
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:46,000
Inşallah, inşallah, Xwedê emrekî dirêj bide.
 
God willing, God willing, may God give you a long life.

659
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:55,000
Silavê min ji miletê Sûr kera, çûçik mezin hene. Çav dûr
dibe, çav nîzîk dibe. Ez çavî giya maç dikim. Xwedê wegiya
bixefilîne.
 
My greetings to the people of Sur (the area), young and old.
Those far and near. I kiss everyone's eyes. May God protect
you all.

660
00:40:55,000 --> 00:41:00,000
Maşallah gundekî bi xêr û bêr e. Wek şebî Kerzelê û Basûtê,
me gav dikin û wa go.
 
Mashallah, it is a village of bounty and blessing. Like the
people of Kerzel and Basût, we walk around and talk.

661
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:05,000
Her kes milkê xwe, xizmetî milkê xwe dike, di erdê xwe da
dişixulin.
 
Everyone serves their property, they work on their land.

662
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:09,000
Jin mêrê xwe dişixulin. Maşallah Xwedê giya bixefilîne.
 
Wives and husbands work together. Mashallah, may God protect
them all.

663
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:14,000
Sata we xweş wela, hemî dişixulin. Xwedê rizqî we bişîne.
 
More power to you really, everyone is working. May God send
you sustenance.

664
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:15,000
Xwedê pê de.
 
God grant it.

665
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:16,000
Xwedê pê de.
 
God grant it.

666
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:17,000
Ne we?
 
Isn't it?

667
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Ekîd lê.
 
Certainly.

668
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Bes kela xew kir, Xwedê nade te.
 
But if you just sleep, God won't give to you.

669
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:25,000
Wela nade. O noka her ro temam derkê, ew jî şixul e, ne we?
 
Indeed He won't. Look now, every day everyone comes out,
that is also work, isn't it?

670
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:26,000
Ew jî şixul e, erê inşallah. Ekîd lê.
 
That is also work, yes God willing. Certainly.

671
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:31,000
Ew jî şixul e. Erê diçe di berê de, di gund de digere. Hişta
em jî pê qorînonî xwe katin e hişta.
 
That is also work. Yes, going to the fields, walking in the
village. Even we have just put our quarantines (referring to
restrictions/work routine) in place.

672
00:41:31,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Her kes bi tiştekî xizmet dike. Yek darê mer dike, yek darê
vedanê, yek darê yopiyê digre.
 
Everyone serves with something. One prunes the trees, one
plants trees, one clears the weeds.

673
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:37,000
Her kes senetê xwe.
 
Everyone has their craft.

674
00:41:37,000 --> 00:41:45,000
Wela senet cem me pirr in xalo. Ez blokan çêdikim, ez
buwaxçî me. Ez vê korî gişî dikim. Ez ji heq gişî têm der
yanî.
 
Well, we have many crafts, uncle. I make cinder blocks, I am
a plasterer. I do all this work. I can handle it all, you
know.

675
00:41:45,000 --> 00:41:48,000
Tu çak behra, îna ka, ez ê ew bikim.
 
You make a living from your share, look now, I will do that.

676
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:49,000
Hîne jî behra dikim, erê.
 
Some also make a living (from agriculture), yes.

677
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:50,000
E dadeka we?
 
Is that your livelihood?

678
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:54,000
Lê ez hem giş korî dikim. Aywa, ez çi korî dêm pêşiya min,
ez ji heq dertêvîm.
 
Yes, I do all kinds of work. Yes, whatever work comes before
me, I handle it.

679
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:58,000
Ê bî, cewxê vê ehdasna bî ye, 7-8 sala jî me kar nekir.
 
So it was, since the time of these events/incidents, for 7-8
years I didn't work.

680
00:41:58,000 --> 00:42:02,000
Ya ono tîçkî ono apê te Hesen got, lawo rabe ser xwe,
bixebite.
 
Then, a little bit, your uncle Hesen said, "Son, stand up,
work."

681
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:07,000
Bira çîçke em ji hev va bin e. E dema go em korîkî xwe
bikin, na mano dilê milet şa kirim, bide mila.
 
Let us be together a bit. When we do our work, not only does
it gladden people's hearts...

682
00:42:07,000 --> 00:42:10,000
Wanê duryela çûne, î binî gundê xwe kirî, bîra mehra xwe
kirî.
 
Those who have gone far away, miss their village base, miss
their lands.

683
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:11,000
Ekîd hene lê.
 
Certainly they do.

684
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:14,000
Em çîçke dilê wan o jî şa bikin, mla çîçke we qehra ji zikê
wan derkeve.
 
Let us gladden their hearts a bit, so that the grief leaves
their stomachs (hearts).

685
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:15,000
Inşallah ewê werin.
 
God willing they will return.

686
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:16,000
Inşallah bi îzna Xwedê.
 
God willing, with God's permission.

687
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:22,000
Menteqe xweş dibe, wela duhem Efrîn sewran pirr xweş bî.
Meşarîa wada dikin, bînayet û...
 
The area will become good, really the second Afrin era will
be very good. They are doing projects there, buildings
and...

688
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:25,000
...kar e bo çêdikin. Ê hoşe hoşe erin bibe.
 
...creating jobs. Slowly, slowly it will get better.

689
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:28,000
De na qulo, ya 10 sal, 15 sal ne, ne we xalo?
 
Don't say that, it's been 10 years, 15 years, hasn't it
uncle?

690
00:42:28,000 --> 00:42:29,000
La qulo ye lê.
 
No, it's not (that long/bad).

691
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:32,000
Lê, di roş av bike to çê nabe. Işt em ke...
 
Yes, you can't build it in a day. Look we...

692
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:34,000
Tengî, me tengî mezin kişandin.
 
Hardship, we endured great hardship.

693
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:40,000
Lê, me tengiya tav mezin, em têra darbas bûn e. Ya em ê noka
elhemdulîlah ji Xwedê ra.
 
Yes, we passed through the greatest of hardships. And now,
praise be to God.

694
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Em ê inşallah wek berê jî biftilin û em ê ji berê rintir
bikin. Em kurmanc cebbar in, cebbar, ne we xalo?
 
We will, God willing, return to how it was before and make
it even better than before. We Kurds are resilient (mighty),
resilient, aren't we uncle?

695
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:48,000
Ekîd em cebbar in ekîd.
 
Certainly we are resilient, certainly.

696
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:50,000
Lê, Xwedê miletê me giya mehfeze ke inşallah.
 
Yes, may God preserve all our people, God willing.

697
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Amîn.
 
Amen.

698
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:53,000
Ka ev kevir na, ev çi kevir na tedîna na?
 
Look at these stones, what kind of stones have you seen
here?

699
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:55,000
Ev kevir na, di vira di til da bûn.
 
These stones, they were here in the hill.

700
00:42:55,000 --> 00:42:56,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

701
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:58,000
Tilek li vir a heye dibên Tilî Kêşûr.
 
There is a hill here they call Keshur Hill.

702
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:58,000
Ji wî tilî, anîn. Til vekirin vira... cehş hûr hatin
vekirin.
 
Yes.

703
00:42:58,000 --> 00:43:05,000
Ji wî tilî, anîn. Til vekirin vira... cehş hûr hatin
vekirin.
 
From that hill, they brought them. They opened the hill
here... they excavated small rocks.

704
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:09,000
Erdê me li vî derê ye. Me jî ra kir hûna hat. Vira heba...
 
Our land is in this place. We lifted them and brought them
here. If it was here...

705
00:43:09,000 --> 00:43:11,000
Ekîd berê kevirê êş bûye heba.
 
Surely this was a millstone before.

706
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:12,000
Abo ye êş bî.
 
It was a mill.

707
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:15,000
Haba berê pê aş digerron, yanî çêkirî ye ev kevir a, ne...
 
Before they would turn the mill with this, meaning this
stone is manufactured (carved), not...

708
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:16,000
Erê ez zanim çêkirî ye.
 
Yes, I know it is carved.

709
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:17,000
Çêkirî ye.
 
It is carved.

710
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Abo ye çêkirî ye.
 
It is carved.

711
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:19,000
Û hav na?
 
And this one?

712
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:22,000
Û hav na jî, berê tê da ew dikutan, genim dikutan.
 
And this one too, before they would pound inside it, they
would pound wheat.

713
00:43:22,000 --> 00:43:23,000
Genim?
 
Wheat?

714
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:23,000
Aywa.
 
Yes.

715
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:24,000
Aywa.
 
Yes.

716
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:25,000
Hek kevir na...
 
This very stone...

717
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Gî genim ne.
 
All wheat.

718
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:27,000
Hav na yê genim ne.
 
This one is for wheat.

719
00:43:27,000 --> 00:43:28,000
Aywa.
 
Yes.

720
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:35,000
Di wir da pirr kevir ne. Ev kevir a jî wekî çû berê
lengik...
 
There are many stones over there. This stone too, like it
went before, a piece of machinery...

721
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:37,000
...Amûda, şûna Amûda, hev kevir a bûn.
 
...the column, the place of the column, were these stones.

722
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:38,000
Hav na jî yê wana bûn erê.
 
These were also theirs, yes.

723
00:43:38,000 --> 00:43:41,000
Xolo însanê berê çiqas cebbar bî, mekin bî.
 
Uncle, the humans of the past were so mighty, strong.

724
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:45,000
Ebo gî çêkirî ye. Gî çêkirî, gî çêkûç çêkirî ne ev na, erê.
 
This is all man-made. All made, all made with hammers, these
ones, yes.

725
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:46,000
Wela însanê berê, mekin bûn.
 
Really, the humans of the past were strong.

726
00:43:46,000 --> 00:43:51,000
Lê, gî çêkirî bûn, ev na jî me çendik hûnan hatin.
 
Yes, they were all made (by hand), these ones too we brought
a few of them here.

727
00:43:51,000 --> 00:43:52,000
Hav jî nefs wekî wana ne?
 
This one is also the same as those?

728
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:55,000
Nefs wekî wana, hav jî wekî wana ye.
 
Same as those, this one is also like those.

729
00:43:55,000 --> 00:43:55,000
Maşallah hêşinahî cem te pirr e maşallah.
 
Yes.

730
00:43:55,000 --> 00:43:58,000
Maşallah hêşinahî cem te pirr e maşallah.
 
Mashallah, you have a lot of greenery here, Mashallah.

731
00:43:58,000 --> 00:44:01,000
Hîn wextî... awê be merro ba hînî xweş ba.
 
At this time... if there was water it would be even nicer.

732
00:44:01,000 --> 00:44:04,000
Wa, maşallah, maşallah.
 
Wow, Mashallah, Mashallah.

733
00:44:04,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Ev na jî darê lêmûnê ne.
 
These are lemon trees.

734
00:44:06,000 --> 00:44:08,000
Maşallah hîn geda te jî hebiye.
 
Mashallah, you have this yard here too.

735
00:44:08,000 --> 00:44:09,000
Erê wela.
 
Yes indeed.

736
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:10,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

737
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:12,000
Ev o, hîn gî dinya ye.
 
This is, all this is the world (meaning it's a large space).

738
00:44:12,000 --> 00:44:16,000
Çi bînî xweş tê xolo, bînî kilkê hingivê, wela xweş ne.
 
What a nice smell comes, uncle, the smell of honeycomb (or
distinct nature smell), really nice.

739
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:17,000
Bînî wî xweş e erê.
 
Its smell is nice, yes.

740
00:44:17,000 --> 00:44:19,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

741
00:44:19,000 --> 00:44:21,000
Wela maşallah çi bînek xweş jê tê.
 
Really Mashallah, what a nice smell comes from it.

742
00:44:21,000 --> 00:44:22,000
Ev o jî lêmûn e.
 
This is also lemon.

743
00:44:22,000 --> 00:44:24,000
Lêmûnê şehrî ye ev o.
 
This is the city lemon (local variety).

744
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:25,000
Ev o şehrî ye na?
 
This is city variety, right?

745
00:44:25,000 --> 00:44:26,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

746
00:44:26,000 --> 00:44:28,000
Aywa, maşallah, maşallah.
 
Yes, Mashallah, Mashallah.

747
00:44:28,000 --> 00:44:30,000
Ev o jî ebû serra ye.
 
And this is cypress ("abu sarra").

748
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:31,000
Oh.
 
Oh.

749
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:33,000
Darê ebû serra... erê, ew jî ebû serra ye.
 
Cypress tree... yes, that is also cypress.

750
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:34,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

751
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:35,000
Ev o yê wî jî ev e?
 
This belongs to him too, this one?

752
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:37,000
Wela hewşek te mezin heye.
 
Really you have a large courtyard.

753
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:39,000
Ev o jî hişînahîm di vira de çînin.
 
And this greenery I plant here.

754
00:44:39,000 --> 00:44:40,000
Rind e.
 
It's good.

755
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:41,000
Çîçke berê mal.
 
A bit of produce for the house.

756
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:42,000
Û heva jî hangar e.
 
And this is a hangar/shed.

757
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:44,000
Bîber heta noka têda hene.
 
There are peppers in it until now.

758
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:45,000
Lewke lê sêrke.
 
Look at the boy there.

759
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:47,000
Lewke lê sêrke erê.
 
Look at the boy, yes.

760
00:44:47,000 --> 00:44:48,000
Lê, hewşê xwe sêrke.
 
Yes, look at your courtyard.

761
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:50,000
Erê hewşê xwe sêrke, hûzan.
 
Yes, look at your courtyard, like this.

762
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:55,000
Birîm hûzan silavê mişteran e heta Almanya jî heta lê, heva
hewşa wa ya, em li hewşa wa ne.
 
Let me say like this, common greetings even to Germany, to
here, this is their courtyard, we are in their courtyard.

763
00:44:55,000 --> 00:44:56,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

764
00:44:56,000 --> 00:44:58,000
Û heva... waxtê xwe çûn e na xalo?
 
And this... their time (season) has passed, right uncle?

765
00:44:58,000 --> 00:45:01,000
Waxtê xwe çûn. Em ê noka helkevin, em ê tişta bidin pêşiya
ne.
 
Their time has passed. We will now dig them up, we will put
things (new crops) in front of them.

766
00:45:01,000 --> 00:45:03,000
Em ê vî şitil em têda de çînin.
 
We will plant these seedlings in it.

767
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:04,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

768
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:07,000
Ji şitil, em tak ro dibin nav erd de çînin.
 
From seedlings, we take them one by one and plant them in
the field.

769
00:45:07,000 --> 00:45:08,000
Nav erd.
 
In the field.

770
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:09,000
Eywa, heva em şitil diçînin.
 
Yes, these seedlings we are planting.

771
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:09,000
Û dilê me xwest, salana heye, em bxod bin da diçînin.
 
Yes.

772
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:12,000
Û dilê me xwest, salana heye, em bxod bin da diçînin.
 
And if our heart desires, there are years, we plant them
under ourselves (meaning nearby/in plots).

773
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:13,000
Wela.
 
Really.

774
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:14,000
E şetwî em diçînin.
 
We plant winter crops.

775
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:15,000
Maşallah Xwedê rizqî we bişîne.
 
Mashallah may God send you sustenance.

776
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:16,000
Amîn.
 
Amen.

777
00:45:16,000 --> 00:45:17,000
Xwedê rizqî we bişîne.
 
God send you sustenance.

778
00:45:17,000 --> 00:45:18,000
Sax be.
 
Be healthy (Thanks).

779
00:45:18,000 --> 00:45:19,000
Ev daro yê çî lê xolo?
 
What are these trees, uncle?

780
00:45:19,000 --> 00:45:20,000
Menzera?
 
Scenery?

781
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:22,000
Havo wanana, darê ji menzera.
 
Those, trees for scenery.

782
00:45:22,000 --> 00:45:24,000
Yanî nadin xwarin, dar nabe.
 
Meaning they don't produce food, they don't become fruit
trees.

783
00:45:24,000 --> 00:45:25,000
Na, menzer.
 
No, scenery.

784
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:26,000
Havo wekî avê xwe wekî çamê, çamê.
 
These are like, like pine, pine.

785
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:28,000
Çilê xwe wekî çamê ye.
 
Its leaves are like pine.

786
00:45:28,000 --> 00:45:29,000
Lê tê xwarin?
 
But is it edible?

787
00:45:29,000 --> 00:45:32,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

788
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:33,000
Xolo çi dar di hewşê ta da ne?
 
Uncle, what trees are in your courtyard?

789
00:45:33,000 --> 00:45:37,000
Ev darana gî me çandin. Ev na... bofka min çandin.
 
These trees, I planted them all. These ones... my father
planted them.

790
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:39,000
Emirê xwe çiqas sal ev daro?
 
How many years old are these trees?

791
00:45:39,000 --> 00:45:41,000
Ev na emrê wana 40 sal e.
 
Their age is 40 years.

792
00:45:41,000 --> 00:45:42,000
40 sal?
 
40 years?

793
00:45:42,000 --> 00:45:43,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

794
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:45,000
A, tîştê wan gelek çêbî ye na xolo?
 
Ah, their growth has been very good, hasn't it uncle?

795
00:45:45,000 --> 00:45:46,000
Gî tî ye ne.
 
They are all full (grown).

796
00:45:46,000 --> 00:45:50,000
Ev na jî, me çandin, wanê jêr.
 
These ones too, we planted, the ones below.

797
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:51,000
E jêr.
 
The ones below.

798
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:54,000
Hav o jî bofka min çand, wanê dît jî me çandin.
 
My father planted this one, and those others we planted.

799
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:55,000
Ev ne wî da jî darê gûzê ne.
 
And inside there are walnut trees.

800
00:45:55,000 --> 00:45:57,000
Havo jî malek kevn e.
 
And this is an old house.

801
00:45:57,000 --> 00:45:58,000
Havo malek kevn e.
 
This is an old house.

802
00:45:58,000 --> 00:45:59,000
Yê wî da, vîsta...
 
Inside it, back then...

803
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:03,000
Berê divir da rût bû, rût, deşt.
 
Before, it was bare here, bare, a plain.

804
00:46:03,000 --> 00:46:05,000
Berê hevo, mala kem bî.
 
Before this, the house was few (or small).

805
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:08,000
Li vira, mal li Sûr kera gahana kî bûn.
 
Here, the houses in the Sur area were clustered.

806
00:46:08,000 --> 00:46:09,000
Berê hewş gahana bî?
 
Before the courtyards were connected?

807
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:10,000
Gahana bîn erê.
 
Connected, yes.

808
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:11,000
Ser pûş bû.
 
It was thatch roofed.

809
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:16,000
Ê rêk tune bû, kareba tune bû. Dilê kesî nedixwest hewşo
bigre.
 
There was no road, no electricity. No one's heart wanted to
take a courtyard.

810
00:46:16,000 --> 00:46:21,000
Ba'dî wê, kareba hat... rêk zift bû.
 
After that, electricity came... the road was paved
(asphalt).

811
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:22,000
Hoşe me mal çêkirin.
 
Then we built the house.

812
00:46:22,000 --> 00:46:24,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

813
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:26,000
...no, qorta em sobit bîn li vî derê.
 
...so, we became established in this place.

814
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:27,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

815
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:29,000
Wela xolo heyat berê xweş bû yan noka xweş e?
 
Well uncle, was life better before or is it better now?

816
00:46:29,000 --> 00:46:32,000
Heyatî berê, no, heyat noka xweş e.
 
Life before, no, life now is better.

817
00:46:32,000 --> 00:46:33,000
Noka xweş e.
 
Now is better.

818
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:34,000
Noka xweş e.
 
Now is better.

819
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:35,000
Ge heye.
 
There is (everything).

820
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Req he bî.
 
There was poverty.

821
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Vir tune bûn.
 
Yes.

822
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:37,000
Vir tune bûn.
 
There were no clothes.

823
00:46:37,000 --> 00:46:38,000
Kuleh tune bûn.
 
There were no hats.

824
00:46:38,000 --> 00:46:39,000
Siqet hebî.
 
There was cold/hardship.

825
00:46:39,000 --> 00:46:39,000
Na.
 
There was hardship.

826
00:46:39,000 --> 00:46:40,000
Na.
 
No.

827
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:41,000
Bes noka gi gi vir vir.
 
But now everything is plentiful.

828
00:46:41,000 --> 00:46:42,000
Ne.
 
No.

829
00:46:42,000 --> 00:46:45,000
Te yekî re got selam eleykum, yanî te be ewk ne, nexoş de be
silava.
 
You said salam alaykum to someone, meaning if not like that,
the greeting would be unpleasant.

830
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:47,000
Gi meslehetê de bî, merheba.
 
It's all about interest (business), hello.

831
00:46:47,000 --> 00:46:48,000
Merheba.
 
Hello.

832
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:49,000
Merheba, erê.
 
Hello, yes.

833
00:46:49,000 --> 00:46:50,000
Berê ne wa bû.
 
It wasn't like that before.

834
00:46:50,000 --> 00:46:51,000
Berê ne wa bî.
 
It wasn't like that before.

835
00:46:51,000 --> 00:46:54,000
Berê siqet hebî, emnîyet hebî, giştek hebî.
 
Before there was trust, security, everything.

836
00:46:54,000 --> 00:46:56,000
Ama noka tiştî wana tune.
 
But now those things don't exist.

837
00:46:56,000 --> 00:46:58,000
Bes heyatî noka ji yê berê qolaytir e.
 
But life now is easier than before.

838
00:46:58,000 --> 00:47:01,000
Makîne tune bûn, derektor tune bûn.
 
There were no machines, no tractors.

839
00:47:01,000 --> 00:47:03,000
Gi li vira bi meşê diçûn racû.
 
Everyone here walked to Rajo.

840
00:47:03,000 --> 00:47:04,000
Meşê?
 
Walking?

841
00:47:04,000 --> 00:47:05,000
Lakan.
 
Of course.

842
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Bes noka...
 
But now...

843
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:10,000
Noka esin derketî, telefon noka te ber Almanya ra da...
 
Now iron (cars) has come out, phones now you talk with
Germany...

844
00:47:10,000 --> 00:47:11,000
Te dibê elo tu televîzyonê dînî lewk.
 
You say hello, you see the boy on television.

845
00:47:11,000 --> 00:47:13,000
Lê, erê.
 
Yes, yes.

846
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:15,000
Tişkê pirr rind e kîbor e.
 
A very good thing, it is great.

847
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:16,000
Pirr ne, erê.
 
Many, yes.

848
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:19,000
Erê teben, hskirnê berê jî rind bî, siqet hebî.
 
Yes of course, the love of the past was also good, there was
trust.

849
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:20,000
Heskrina ba rind bî, naam.
 
That love was good, yes.

850
00:47:20,000 --> 00:47:21,000
Pirr xweş bî.
 
It was very nice.

851
00:47:21,000 --> 00:47:22,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

852
00:47:22,000 --> 00:47:24,000
Maşallah, çi dar ne.
 
Mashallah, what trees.

853
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:24,000
Maşallah, maşallah.
 
Yes.

854
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:26,000
Maşallah, maşallah.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

855
00:47:26,000 --> 00:47:28,000
Li hewşa xalo bigre, hewşa xalo bigre.
 
Film the uncle's courtyard, film the uncle's courtyard.

856
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:29,000
Hewşa xalo bigre.
 
Film the uncle's courtyard.

857
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:30,000
Xolo, ez...
 
Uncle, I...

858
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:32,000
Wer vira Hesen.
 
Come here Hesen.

859
00:47:32,000 --> 00:47:33,000
Ew kî ye?
 
Who is that?

860
00:47:33,000 --> 00:47:33,000
Te nav lê kirî Hesen?
 
Hesen.

861
00:47:33,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Te nav lê kirî Hesen?
 
You named him Hesen?

862
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:37,000
Hesen wer vira.
 
Hesen come here.

863
00:47:37,000 --> 00:47:38,000
Hesen.
 
Hesen.

864
00:47:38,000 --> 00:47:39,000
Hesen wer vira.
 
Hesen come here.

865
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:40,000
Wer vira.
 
Come here.

866
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:41,000
Wer.
 
Come.

867
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:43,000
Tu xêr qeriyayî?
 
Are you frozen/scared?

868
00:47:43,000 --> 00:47:44,000
De wer.
 
Come on.

869
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:45,000
Wer.
 
Come.

870
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:48,000
Liko kemîra ta dikşîne, liko liko, wer wer.
 
Look the camera is filming you, look look, come come.

871
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:50,000
De wer kemîra te dikşîne wer wer.
 
Come on, the camera is filming you, come come.

872
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:52,000
Xolo wela te qîmetê zanê.
 
Uncle, really you know the value.

873
00:47:52,000 --> 00:47:53,000
Wer wer.
 
Come come.

874
00:47:53,000 --> 00:47:55,000
Min got te qîmetê zanê.
 
I said you know the value.

875
00:47:55,000 --> 00:47:57,000
Liko liko liko liko kemîra ye, kemîra ye binêre.
 
Look look look look it's a camera, it's a camera look.

876
00:47:57,000 --> 00:47:59,000
Gerek tu tiştê xweş pê dê ho.
 
You must give him something good.

877
00:47:59,000 --> 00:48:00,000
Lê.
 
Yes.

878
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:01,000
Ez mist didimê.
 
I give him yogurt.

879
00:48:01,000 --> 00:48:01,000
Mist û şîr erê.
 
Yogurt?

880
00:48:01,000 --> 00:48:03,000
Mist û şîr erê.
 
Yogurt and milk, yes.

881
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:03,000
Rind e, pisî rind in na.
 
Here here.

882
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Rind e, pisî rind in na.
 
It's good, cats are good, right.

883
00:48:06,000 --> 00:48:08,000
Liko liko liko, pisîkê vî gundî ne.
 
Look look look, the cats of this village.

884
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:12,000
Lê, manê dû mişko, mişko tiştê wano bar nade, digre.
 
Yes, meaning regarding mice, mice and such things, he
doesn't let them go, he catches them.

885
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:14,000
Xolo, ekî suwalek ji te pirskem.
 
Uncle, let me ask you a question.

886
00:48:14,000 --> 00:48:19,000
Noka ez pirr, ez pirr mala dikevim ê, ha wekî vê hênik nîn
e, çima hênik e?
 
Now I enter many houses, but none are cool like this one,
why is it cool?

887
00:48:19,000 --> 00:48:21,000
Ev no manê çine? Çi manê dide?
 
What is the meaning of this? What does it mean?

888
00:48:21,000 --> 00:48:22,000
Ev no berê digotin manê nezerê.
 
Before they said this meant the "evil eye" (or a charm
against it).

889
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:23,000
Nezerê.
 
The evil eye.

890
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:26,000
Ev o manê nezerê, yanî...
 
This means the evil eye, meaning...

891
00:48:26,000 --> 00:48:28,000
Tûrîstî kevin e yanî. Berê da hevo bimayî.
 
It's an old artifact, meaning. It remained from the past.

892
00:48:28,000 --> 00:48:29,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

893
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:31,000
Manê nezerê erê.
 
Meaning the evil eye, yes.

894
00:48:31,000 --> 00:48:33,000
Ka em hinekî mor e, em hinekî lextokî jûr va jî bikşînin.
 
Let us move a bit, let's film a bit from upstairs too.

895
00:48:33,000 --> 00:48:35,000
Wer.
 
Come.

896
00:48:35,000 --> 00:48:37,000
Maşallah, maşallah.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

897
00:48:37,000 --> 00:48:44,000
Çi gundekî xweş e.
 
What a beautiful village.

898
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:47,000
Wela xol, tizanê min nêt heye hewşek xo ke çêkim.
 
Really uncle, you know I have an intention to build myself a
courtyard like this.

899
00:48:47,000 --> 00:48:50,000
Te til diye, temam byorkî kêlek tila.
 
You've seen the hill, exactly beside the hill.

900
00:48:50,000 --> 00:48:53,000
Wela yî çi cî o der e. Bi avê va nîzîk.
 
Really what a place that is. Close to the water.

901
00:48:53,000 --> 00:48:56,000
Ez dahatim wir derê, tim min digot ez ê werim ono...
 
I was coming there, I always said I would come...

902
00:48:56,000 --> 00:48:59,000
Û dav xo bigrim, mano avî ne, war xwar, ser pişta xên e.
 
And take that spot, meaning it's watery, come down, it's on
the back of the house.

903
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:01,000
Em li wir erdê kî li wir heye.
 
We have a piece of land there.

904
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:02,000
Em cîranê hevin de.
 
We are neighbors then.

905
00:49:02,000 --> 00:49:03,000
Gî nîzîkî hevin, nîzîkî hevin.
 
We are all close to each other, close to each other.

906
00:49:03,000 --> 00:49:04,000
Eceb o dî.
 
That's amazing.

907
00:49:04,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Wela xweş e wi derê, xweş e ê.
 
Really it is nice there, it is nice.

908
00:49:06,000 --> 00:49:07,000
Erê wela.
 
Yes indeed.

909
00:49:07,000 --> 00:49:09,000
Viro Sûrke ye.
 
Here is the Sûrke (border fence).

910
00:49:09,000 --> 00:49:10,000
Û honikî hidûd e.
 
And there is the border.

911
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:11,000
E, têl va bo nîzîk e têl binêre.
 
Ah, the wire is close with this, look at the wire.

912
00:49:11,000 --> 00:49:13,000
Em hidûdî Tirko da ne, liko sêrke.
 
We are at the Turkish border, look see.

913
00:49:13,000 --> 00:49:14,000
Wela.
 
Really.

914
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:18,000
Erê ev o na ve derê Sûrke jî di ber têlê da ye.
 
Yes, this here, the Sûrke is also along the wire.

915
00:49:18,000 --> 00:49:21,000
Min go Sûrke di ber têlê da ye, têl ma bo nîzîk e.
 
I said the Sûrke is along the wire, the wire is close to us.

916
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:22,000
Ho liko.
 
There look.

917
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:24,000
Xolo kîlometre kî heye? Tune ne?
 
Uncle is it a kilometer? No right?

918
00:49:24,000 --> 00:49:27,000
Na, toliya gir, dused metre ye.
 
No, the length of the hill, it is two hundred meters.

919
00:49:27,000 --> 00:49:28,000
Nêzîk in, pirr nêzîk in.
 
We are close, very close.

920
00:49:28,000 --> 00:49:31,000
Ew berê çîmê wî derê mûsî, ew berê wî dorna pirr çûme.
 
That side, the meadow of that place... I have gone to that
side often.

921
00:49:31,000 --> 00:49:31,000
Rêk camo le îmet ro dare.
 
Yes.

922
00:49:31,000 --> 00:49:32,000
Rêk camo le îmet ro dare.
 
The road is right next to it.

923
00:49:32,000 --> 00:49:34,000
Ji ma vî de dused metre ye.
 
From us here it is two hundred meters.

924
00:49:34,000 --> 00:49:35,000
A.
 
Ah.

925
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:37,000
Av di ber o dare zoter?
 
The water runs in front of it?

926
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:40,000
Xolo têbê wextî ne, av divir o jî diçû ne, pêşî mala te re.
 
Uncle, you say at that time, water flowed here too, right,
in front of your house.

927
00:49:40,000 --> 00:49:43,000
Di vir e de biro, av hofî di vira de meşê.
 
From here brother, the water would flow from right here.

928
00:49:43,000 --> 00:49:45,000
Eywa, ew av a ji kanîyê tê.
 
Yes, that water comes from the spring.

929
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:49,000
Di vira ji kanîyê tê, ji ber malê tê, ji tev avê reş... tev
ev dit vira tên.
 
Here it comes from the spring, comes from in front of the
house, from the black water... they all come here.

930
00:49:49,000 --> 00:49:51,000
Û dipşê malê tar û diro dare.
 
And it passes in front of the house and goes there.

931
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:53,000
Di vira dare, pê vî erdî av didin.
 
It goes here, they water this land with it.

932
00:49:53,000 --> 00:49:54,000
Wela.
 
Really.

933
00:49:54,000 --> 00:49:55,000
Erê, av erd ana ho da bo bin.
 
Yes, these lands were irrigated.

934
00:49:55,000 --> 00:49:58,000
Çiqsa hano heyat kî xweş e, ana av dipşê malê tar o jî bar
ke.
 
Such a nice life, that water passes in front of your house
and you let it go.

935
00:49:58,000 --> 00:49:59,000
Derke.
 
Comes out.

936
00:49:59,000 --> 00:50:00,000
Maşallah a vlî me war vî hewş...
 
Mashallah look at this courtyard...

937
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:02,000
Noş gîyan, nîzîk bika.
 
Bon appétit, bring it closer.

938
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:09,000
Maşalo.
 
Mashallah.

939
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:12,000
Maşalo, berxekî ciwan e.
 
Mashallah, it is a beautiful lamb.

940
00:50:12,000 --> 00:50:17,000
Ka? Yê nêr e, hewa yê mê ye, hewa yê min are.
 
Which one? That is a male, this is a female, this is mine,
yes.

941
00:50:17,000 --> 00:50:19,000
Hewa mê ye.
 
This is a female.

942
00:50:19,000 --> 00:50:21,000
Pzê te li çolê ye?
 
Is your sheep flock out in the wilderness?

943
00:50:21,000 --> 00:50:24,000
Pzê darê, çolê ye, êvarê tê.
 
The flock is outside, in the wilderness, it comes back in
the evening.

944
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:28,000
Êvarê sibe em êm dikin, ê îvarê were jê em êm dikin, berxî
gendişî li konê ne.
 
In the evening... in the morning we feed them, and in the
evening when they come back we feed them, the lambs remain
in the tent.

945
00:50:28,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Ev berxê xwe ne.
 
These are its lambs.

946
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:31,000
Maşalo.
 
Mashallah.

947
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:33,000
Rind e.
 
It is good.

948
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:35,000
Maşalo çi cawekî xweş e.
 
Mashallah, what a nice place.

949
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:37,000
We qozana te kişand, qozan jî bikşîn.
 
You filmed the handsome ones, film the handsome ones too.

950
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:39,000
Qoz lê?
 
Handsome, right?

951
00:50:39,000 --> 00:50:43,000
Maşalo, maşalo. Ha ev işta miletî sûrke?
 
Mashallah, mashallah. Look, is this the red sheep people
talk about?

952
00:50:43,000 --> 00:50:45,000
Ha mana îşaretê me ev e.
 
Yes, look, our mark is this.

953
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Gando, sa ke.
 
Look at the Gando (plant/grass).

954
00:50:46,000 --> 00:50:48,000
Tûlik li ver pir e meşhûr e, tûlikê dixwin?
 
Is there a lot of mallow (tûlik) around here? Is it famous?
Do they eat mallow?

955
00:50:48,000 --> 00:50:49,000
Na, tûlik...
 
No, mallow...

956
00:50:49,000 --> 00:50:50,000
Em dibên pincar.
 
We call it "pincar" (beet/greens).

957
00:50:50,000 --> 00:50:51,000
Pincar, are.
 
Pincar, yes.

958
00:50:51,000 --> 00:50:52,000
Pir xelk dibê pincar.
 
Many people say "pincar".

959
00:50:52,000 --> 00:50:55,000
Sa ke pazê gîya dixwe, her malekê pazê xwe heye.
 
Look, the sheep eats grass, every household has their own
sheep.

960
00:50:55,000 --> 00:50:56,000
Xo li çil cimo hene, çil?
 
Does the flock consist of forty, forty?

961
00:50:56,000 --> 00:51:00,000
Çil hene ya, malekê hewandi, malê brakê min yek hewandi.
 
Yes, there are forty, one household has them, my brother's
household has some.

962
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:01,000
Çil?
 
Forty?

963
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:02,000
Çil hene, are.
 
There are forty, yes.

964
00:51:02,000 --> 00:51:03,000
Gî ne hewandi ya?
 
Does everyone have them?

965
00:51:03,000 --> 00:51:04,000
Ekserî hekê paz e cimo?
 
Is it mostly sheep with this group?

966
00:51:04,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Ekserî paz û bizin in ho.
 
Mostly sheep and goats, yes.

967
00:51:06,000 --> 00:51:08,000
Maşalo, maşalo, Xudê rizqê gîya bişîne.
 
Mashallah, mashallah, may God send sustenance to everyone.

968
00:51:08,000 --> 00:51:11,000
Amîn, ji te ra jî kekê.
 
Amen, for you as well, brother.

969
00:51:11,000 --> 00:51:13,000
Ere ere, ka bişîne ka xwe da, xo ke tal ne.
 
Yes yes, send it, come on, don't be bitter (upset).

970
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:18,000
Were were hissê xwe bişîj gender, were.
 
Come, come, wash your feelings (relax) with them, come.

971
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:19,000
Maşalo.
 
Mashallah.

972
00:51:19,000 --> 00:51:23,000
Ê ko pazê te heye, keriyê te jî tûne ye?
 
So, you have sheep, but don't you have a herd (large flock)?

973
00:51:23,000 --> 00:51:27,000
Gerek keriyê te hebe, edetê çoyê hebe.
 
You should have a herd, you should have the shepherd's staff
custom.

974
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:30,000
Çoyê te tûne ye, bila me?
 
You don't have a staff, tell me?

975
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:33,000
Xaltîkê dibên bila me çoyê te tûne ye.
 
Auntie says tell me, you don't have a staff.

976
00:51:33,000 --> 00:51:36,000
Şivanî me ezbî çoyê xwe heye, keriyê xwe heye, na we?
 
Our shepherd... usually has his staff, has his herd, right?

977
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:38,000
Şivanî... Şivanî mal e ev o.
 
Shepherd... This is a household shepherd.

978
00:51:38,000 --> 00:51:39,000
Aaa şivanî mal e.
 
Ah, a household shepherd.

979
00:51:39,000 --> 00:51:41,000
Pazê xwe berde diçêrin.
 
He releases his sheep and they graze.

980
00:51:41,000 --> 00:51:43,000
Aaa maşalo, Xudê emirê ke dirêj bide.
 
Ah mashallah, may God give you a long life.

981
00:51:43,000 --> 00:51:45,000
Maşalo, maşalo, ev trî reşik e xolu?
 
Mashallah, mashallah, is this one a black breed (Reşik),
uncle?

982
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:47,000
Abo tirî na, Himsî ye.
 
No not that breed, it is Hamsi.

983
00:51:47,000 --> 00:51:48,000
Himsî ye?
 
Hamsi?

984
00:51:48,000 --> 00:51:48,000
Maşalo.
 
It is Hamsi.

985
00:51:48,000 --> 00:51:50,000
Maşalo.
 
Mashallah.

986
00:51:50,000 --> 00:51:51,000
Trî Himsî ye.
 
Hamsi breed.

987
00:51:51,000 --> 00:51:53,000
Evana ge bele qarn ne bî yo, na?
 
These ones don't have horns, right?

988
00:51:53,000 --> 00:51:56,000
Evana bele qarn ne bî nam didim pêz e, erê.
 
These don't have horns... yes.

989
00:51:56,000 --> 00:51:57,000
Ê paz pê nayeşe? Belo?
 
And the sheep don't get sick? Without horns?

990
00:51:57,000 --> 00:51:58,000
No, tş nabe, bas e.
 
No, nothing happens, it's good.

991
00:51:58,000 --> 00:51:59,000
Aaa.
 
I see.

992
00:51:59,000 --> 00:52:00,000
Maşalo.
 
Mashallah.

993
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:08,000
Ta ta ta ta ta.
 
Ta ta ta ta ta (Calling birds/chickens).

994
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:09,000
Ta ta.
 
Ta ta.

995
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:11,000
Xolu ge hêlîna dikin?
 
Uncle, do they make nests (lay eggs)?

996
00:52:11,000 --> 00:52:12,000
Hindik tina dikin.
 
They do a little bit.

997
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:13,000
Maşalo.
 
Mashallah.

998
00:52:13,000 --> 00:52:14,000
Ta.
 
Ta.

999
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:15,000
Ba wana evana xolu?
 
Are these yours, uncle?

1000
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:16,000
Ta.
 
Ta.

1001
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:18,000
Min go ba wana?
 
I said, are they yours?

1002
00:52:18,000 --> 00:52:19,000
Erê ba wana.
 
Yes, they are ours.

1003
00:52:19,000 --> 00:52:21,000
Ha ryek biçin evana?
 
Do they go anywhere (wander off)?

1004
00:52:21,000 --> 00:52:27,000
Wela evana ha ryek... me jor e na firutine, bes îşta zêde
dibin, ahbaba nadin, cîrana nadin, me na firutine evana.
 
Well, they don't go... we haven't sold the ones up top, they
just increase, we give to friends, we give to neighbors, we
haven't sold these.

1005
00:52:27,000 --> 00:52:28,000
Eywa.
 
I see.

1006
00:52:28,000 --> 00:52:29,000
Xolu dibê...
 
Uncle says...

1007
00:52:29,000 --> 00:52:35,000
Evana... soq in, nakevin der, li derva xew dikin, berf,
baran li derva xew dikin.
 
These... are hardy (cold-resistant), they don't go inside,
they sleep outside, in snow, in rain, they sleep outside.

1008
00:52:35,000 --> 00:52:39,000
Xolu dibê rind ne, dibê wekî kûşk a rûniştinê, dibê dizar...
dizar o?
 
Uncle says they are good, he says like sitting in a mansion,
he says the porch... the porch?

1009
00:52:39,000 --> 00:52:43,000
We kûşk o ne, li ber xew dikin, berqê pilleko xew dikin, na
rin hewşê.
 
Like a mansion, they sleep in front of it, they sleep on the
steps of the stairs, they don't go into the courtyard.

1010
00:52:43,000 --> 00:52:46,000
Dibê wextî pejnê tişkî bikin, dizo bikin, derke bon dikin.
 
He says when they sense something, sense a thief, they go
out and make noise.

1011
00:52:46,000 --> 00:52:48,000
Kûk xew nakin evana, pir sohî ne.
 
They don't sleep deeply (roots/soundly), they are very
alert.

1012
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:49,000
Rind e.
 
Good.

1013
00:52:49,000 --> 00:52:51,000
Û nakevin hindir.
 
And they don't fall inside (go indoors).

1014
00:52:51,000 --> 00:52:52,000
Eywa.
 
I see.

1015
00:52:52,000 --> 00:52:55,000
Di derva j vistan û havînê, berf bê ke, çi lê ke, wul viderê
dima xelîn.
 
Outside in winter and summer, let snow come, whatever
happens, they stay right there.

1016
00:52:55,000 --> 00:52:55,000
Nakevin hindir.
 
I see.

1017
00:52:55,000 --> 00:52:56,000
Nakevin hindir.
 
They don't go inside.

1018
00:52:56,000 --> 00:52:57,000
Wekî herezan e.
 
They are like guards.

1019
00:52:57,000 --> 00:52:59,000
Erê wekî herezan e, îvarê bon dikin.
 
Yes, like guards, in the evening they make noise.

1020
00:52:59,000 --> 00:53:01,000
Lê îvarê xşm dikin, bes pejnê tişkî...
 
But in the evening they get angry, only if they sense
something...

1021
00:53:01,000 --> 00:53:02,000
Pejnê tişkî... di rinde podixin.
 
Sense something... they protect well.

1022
00:53:02,000 --> 00:53:02,000
Erê herezan e.
 
Sense something.

1023
00:53:02,000 --> 00:53:03,000
Erê herezan e.
 
Yes, they are guards.

1024
00:53:03,000 --> 00:53:04,000
Lê maşalo.
 
But mashallah.

1025
00:53:04,000 --> 00:53:06,000
We hes kiriye hene pejnê tişkî kirî?
 
Have you felt it, when they sensed something?

1026
00:53:06,000 --> 00:53:07,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

1027
00:53:07,000 --> 00:53:08,000
Xeterîk heye?
 
Is there any danger?

1028
00:53:08,000 --> 00:53:10,000
Xeterîk heye zane.
 
They know there is danger.

1029
00:53:10,000 --> 00:53:12,000
Emrî vana çend meh e kekê?
 
How many months old are these, brother?

1030
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:16,000
Emrî vana, hinek di meh ekin, hinek meh ekin, hinek di meh û
nîv in.
 
Their age, some are two months, some are one month, some are
two and a half months.

1031
00:53:16,000 --> 00:53:18,000
Têda wana jê hene, wana jê hene.
 
There are those kinds among them, and those kinds among
them.

1032
00:53:18,000 --> 00:53:20,000
A maşalo, maşalo.
 
Ah mashallah, mashallah.

1033
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:21,000
Girûkê nabînin.
 
They don't look like they have mange.

1034
00:53:21,000 --> 00:53:22,000
Girûkê nabînin, na.
 
They don't have mange, no.

1035
00:53:22,000 --> 00:53:24,000
Pşşş girûkê nabînin, erê.
 
Pshhh, they don't have mange, yes.

1036
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:29,000
Maşalo avana çi barxek na rindik na. Welû îmam sîretkî xo
nov dikşînin, were hê hê.
 
Mashallah, these are such nice lambs. Let's take a picture
of ourselves with them, come hey hey.

1037
00:53:29,000 --> 00:53:31,000
Çoso kîbar ne, gelê?
 
How elegant they are, right?

1038
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:36,000
Me jî wextkî hewandin, bes min wela me têda ziror kir, min
neha mîlyon weraq têda kirin ziror.
 
We also raised them at one time, but honestly I lost money
on them, I lost nine million bills on them.

1039
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:38,000
Coko... ba biye.
 
Because... it happened.

1040
00:53:38,000 --> 00:53:39,000
Çowrî jî te nebî.
 
Even if you don't have a shepherd.

1041
00:53:39,000 --> 00:53:42,000
Ê me pê nekanî, maşalo, xolu avo yekî rindik e fantoz e.
 
We couldn't handle it, mashallah, uncle this is a nice one,
fantastic.

1042
00:53:42,000 --> 00:53:44,000
Pşşş.
 
Pshhh.

1043
00:53:44,000 --> 00:53:46,000
Maşalo, maşalo.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

1044
00:53:46,000 --> 00:53:49,000
Avana ta jî çoso rind a gindik o, hey hey, li mî?
 
This one of yours is also so nice and chunky, hey hey, look
at me?

1045
00:53:49,000 --> 00:53:52,000
Gî darink e? Darin cem dê kê.
 
Are they all enclosed? Enclosed near the mother.

1046
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:54,000
Aaa, pşşş.
 
I see, pshhh.

1047
00:53:54,000 --> 00:53:55,000
Avana jî...
 
These ones too...

1048
00:53:55,000 --> 00:53:56,000
Pşşş.
 
Pshhh.

1049
00:53:56,000 --> 00:53:58,000
Pşşş.
 
Pshhh.

1050
00:53:58,000 --> 00:54:00,000
Eh.
 
Eh.

1051
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:02,000
Îşta... ana ana teze rindik in o.
 
Look... these are fresh and nice, look.

1052
00:54:02,000 --> 00:54:04,000
Lêmî were, ho lêmî were.
 
Come to me, hey come to me.

1053
00:54:04,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Yekî xwo bigire, yekî xwo bigire, yekî xwo bigire.
 
Catch one, catch one, catch one.

1054
00:54:06,000 --> 00:54:08,000
Ê konê bigire, zaza bigire yekî bigire.
 
Catch one inside the tent, quickly catch one.

1055
00:54:08,000 --> 00:54:09,000
Bigire yekî.
 
Catch one.

1056
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:10,000
De bigire yekî.
 
Come on, catch one.

1057
00:54:10,000 --> 00:54:11,000
Bigire yekî.
 
Catch one.

1058
00:54:11,000 --> 00:54:12,000
De bigire.
 
Come on, catch it.

1059
00:54:12,000 --> 00:54:13,000
Yekî xwo bigire.
 
Catch one yourself.

1060
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:14,000
Ne konê bigire.
 
No, catch it in the tent.

1061
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:15,000
De ti konê bigire de.
 
Come on, catch it in the tent then.

1062
00:54:15,000 --> 00:54:17,000
De bigire.
 
Come on, catch it.

1063
00:54:17,000 --> 00:54:19,000
Bigire, ne konê ne.
 
Catch it, not inside the tent.

1064
00:54:19,000 --> 00:54:21,000
Maşalo, maşalo.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

1065
00:54:21,000 --> 00:54:25,000
Avana jî baran e, û bizin e.
 
These are rams, and goats.

1066
00:54:25,000 --> 00:54:29,000
Avana naxoş in, mil mol êştin, pazî didare darvo, çûle.
 
These are sick, with joint pain/limping, the sheep were
outside, in the pasture.

1067
00:54:29,000 --> 00:54:31,000
Avana jî tebeqe.
 
These also have Foot and Mouth Disease (Tebeq).

1068
00:54:31,000 --> 00:54:32,000
Tebeq e?
 
Foot and Mouth Disease?

1069
00:54:32,000 --> 00:54:32,000
We derman didayê?
 
Yes, Foot and Mouth Disease.

1070
00:54:32,000 --> 00:54:33,000
We derman didayê?
 
Did you give them medicine?

1071
00:54:33,000 --> 00:54:36,000
We derman didayê, îja lingî wa kuli ye.
 
I gave them medicine, so their feet are infected.

1072
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:37,000
Dişîn yan derman didinê?
 
Do you wash them or give them medicine?

1073
00:54:37,000 --> 00:54:38,000
Derman didinê.
 
We give them medicine.

1074
00:54:38,000 --> 00:54:41,000
Belingî gendi kût ketye sos e naxoşî kî lêket.
 
Their legs are struck with numbness/pain, a sickness struck
them.

1075
00:54:41,000 --> 00:54:42,000
Tabak na? Kûtbîn e.
 
Not Tebeq? Just numbness/stiffness.

1076
00:54:42,000 --> 00:54:43,000
Kûtbîn e, mil mol êştin e, erê.
 
Numbness, joint pain, yes.

1077
00:54:43,000 --> 00:54:45,000
Xolu ne dikin moz û tenikî genda?
 
Uncle, don't you put bananas and tins (splints/remedies) on
them?

1078
00:54:45,000 --> 00:54:48,000
No, derman heye, liko derman heye lê dixim.
 
No, there is medicine, I have a spray medicine I apply.

1079
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:48,000
Maşalo, maşalo.
 
Did you go to the veterinary doctor?

1080
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:49,000
Maşalo, maşalo.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

1081
00:54:49,000 --> 00:54:52,000
Avana çoso hinik şîrîn na rindik na lebna.
 
These are so sweet and nice [looking].

1082
00:54:52,000 --> 00:54:53,000
Ta ecibandin?
 
Did you like them?

1083
00:54:53,000 --> 00:54:55,000
Hê?
 
Huh?

1084
00:54:55,000 --> 00:54:57,000
Avo dermonê gendi ye.
 
This is their medicine.

1085
00:54:57,000 --> 00:55:00,000
Taben dewar jî te hewan, hesren...
 
So you kept livestock, strictly...

1086
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:03,000
Dermonî genda gike cem te hebe.
 
You should have their medicine with you.

1087
00:55:03,000 --> 00:55:05,000
Avo jî bax e, el linga dikim avo.
 
This is a spray, I apply this to the legs.

1088
00:55:05,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Ê, mehnîye tebeq e.
 
Yes, meaning it is Foot and Mouth Disease.

1089
00:55:06,000 --> 00:55:08,000
Mehnî tebeqî ye, erê avo.
 
Meaning it is Foot and Mouth Disease, yes this is it.

1090
00:55:08,000 --> 00:55:11,000
Ere, taben derman tûm bi tûm heye, sehlleb heye, na?
 
Yes, so there is medicine for everything, there is Salep
(remedy), right?

1091
00:55:11,000 --> 00:55:13,000
Hevo îltîhab e.
 
This is for inflammation.

1092
00:55:13,000 --> 00:55:14,000
Îltîhab e?
 
Inflammation?

1093
00:55:14,000 --> 00:55:18,000
Û hav jî... lo no hevo bixos xûnê tê ye, hevo jî î sxûnê ye.
 
And this one too... no look this one is for hot blood
(fever), this one is for cold (pain/rheumatism).

1094
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:19,000
Mm.
 
Mm.

1095
00:55:19,000 --> 00:55:22,000
Taben jema tixirî bayterî heye li Racû?
 
So, is there a veterinary doctor near us in Rajo?

1096
00:55:22,000 --> 00:55:25,000
Ji Racû tînin. Naxoşî pêz hewal didin?
 
You bring them from Rajo. Do they treat sheep sicknesses?

1097
00:55:25,000 --> 00:55:30,000
Tuxtir hene livra, tuxtir hene, û îlacî pêş o serî meryo
heye, pirr e.
 
There are doctors here, doctors, and sheep medicine is
available over the heads of men (abundant), lots of it.

1098
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:31,000
Pirr e, erê.
 
Lots of it, yes.

1099
00:55:31,000 --> 00:55:35,000
Maşalo.
 
Mashallah.

1100
00:55:35,000 --> 00:55:39,000
Serke, mogo lokî ta serke, hemî nav barxek o dano, ono.
 
Release it, I said man release it, look at the name
(appearance) of the lamb, like that.

1101
00:55:39,000 --> 00:55:41,000
Fehm dî ye?
 
Did you understand?

1102
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:44,000
Maşalo.
 
Mashallah.

1103
00:55:44,000 --> 00:55:46,000
Xolu ta se piştî vono xê zerik kirî?
 
Uncle why did you paint their backs yellow?

1104
00:55:46,000 --> 00:55:51,000
Avno... dêkê genda, dêk tine ye, me bêlik kirî, menê hewa
dêkê genda mirî yabo.
 
These... their mother, there is no mother, we marked them,
meaning their mother is dead.

1105
00:55:51,000 --> 00:55:52,000
Dêkê xo mirî ye?
 
Their mother is dead?

1106
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:53,000
Dêkê xo mirî ye, erê.
 
Their mother is dead, yes.

1107
00:55:53,000 --> 00:55:54,000
Ê, û ta bêlik kirî.
 
Ah, and you marked them.

1108
00:55:54,000 --> 00:55:58,000
Menê bêlik be, hewa... menê em zonibûn kijon... menê
bimjînin... a wa dimjînin.
 
Meaning marked, that... meaning so we know which one...
meaning to suckle... ah so they suckle.

1109
00:55:58,000 --> 00:55:59,000
Ê, bi xincî têdin?
 
Ah, do they come with force (to nurse)?

1110
00:55:59,000 --> 00:56:01,000
Bi xincî genda têdin, erê.
 
They come with their force, yes.

1111
00:56:01,000 --> 00:56:02,000
Aaa.
 
I see.

1112
00:56:02,000 --> 00:56:03,000
Rind e, maşalo rindikin e.
 
Good, mashallah they are nice.

1113
00:56:03,000 --> 00:56:04,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

1114
00:56:04,000 --> 00:56:05,000
Bêdş na we?
 
Milking, right?

1115
00:56:05,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Bêdş, qon bimeşin rind e.
 
Milking, walking them is good.

1116
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:07,000
Lê bimeşin rind e.
 
Yes, walking them is good.

1117
00:56:07,000 --> 00:56:10,000
Lênû şîr dixun tştî şîr xoş e, gerek çiq bimeşin.
 
Because they drink milk, milk is good, they must walk a bit.

1118
00:56:10,000 --> 00:56:11,000
Xolu çend neqilkî didzin?
 
Uncle how many times do you milk them?

1119
00:56:11,000 --> 00:56:12,000
Di neqlo.
 
Two times.

1120
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:14,000
Di neqlo didzê? Sak bikef bê di neqlo didzê?
 
You milk two times? Even if you are happy (relaxed) you milk
two times?

1121
00:56:14,000 --> 00:56:18,000
Sak kêf bê di neqlo didzê, amo... gi eqintî bê neqilkê
didzê.
 
Even if happy we milk two times, but... if it is scarce we
milk one time.

1122
00:56:18,000 --> 00:56:20,000
Neqilkê, xolu ta el viderê xê kiriye?
 
